## Portier Port Management

Before starting ANY dev server, run `portier scan --json` to check port conflicts.

### If port 3000/5173/8080 is already in use:
1. Run `portier assign . --range 3000-4000` to get free ports
2. This auto-detects your project stack and assigns free ports
3. Updates config files automatically

Instead of running commands directly, use:
```
portier run -- npm run dev
portier run -- python manage.py runserver
portier run -- cargo run
```
This prevents EADDRINUSE errors transparently.

### Setup:
```bash
# One-time setup:
portier link   # register this project
portier config init  # init project config
portier daemon --install  # enable background auto-healer
```
